    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_4b8f6b76e270672b1f2a43225fab0a8c392a382a1c71debf6011f6a2c7ebb232",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "A positive-dimensional common-period fixed set can force a lower bound on long-range counting fluctuations in the stated closed-surface setting. Separately, nonarithmetic triangles can show finite-range exponential length-multiplicity fits while retaining GOE spacings, and under the source's asymptotic ansatz the diagonal form factor reaches order one only at the arithmetic rate λ=1/2. Fixed-set dimension, asymptotic multiplicity rate, Hecke labels, and Jacquet–Langlands transfer must therefore be audited as distinct structures.",
