      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_5d015a779aa9d7b8a7c50602090bd9a59afc90d08561a9ba23b0ee5edc4972e6",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "Regularized Hadamard factorization formally decomposes the global symbol ξ(1/2+i□) into zero-indexed local second-order factors, while a pseudo-Hermitian similarity formally exposes dilation-type representatives behind a nonlocal difference Hamiltonian. Both make simpler local expressions visible, but reassembly of a factorized functional calculus and transport through a similarity map are different operations with different analytic obligations.",
