    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_6be259964ac40ca60b7c47972518fc31a5e0fbcb3c27c628ce83ce84684a1a6d",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "For v(x)p, the travel-time coordinate q=∫dx/v(x) leaves a weighted plane-wave formal solution; an ε-scaled finite difference formally tends to a dilation representative; and a quantization inheriting five classical Noether generators can still have continuous spectrum. A separate proposed phase-space boundary is what is claimed to discretize dilation, so simple dynamics and preserved symmetry do not determine spectral type without admissibility and domain data.",
