    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_7b854914556a74ca0f2c779cf84ed034f9d050c9fbab1d24da5d0bdc71537fe4",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "Explicit-formula programs reuse harmonic probes to place spectral and arithmetic data in one comparison, but the resulting proof burdens differ: Weil's test family requires positivity for every admissible probe; Montgomery's continuation past unit frequency requires main-order control of shifted von Mangoldt correlations; and the local trace model requires the transverse fixed-point weight |1-λ|^(-1) together with separate treatment of λ=1.",
