    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_8a2de8da46cc2ad1370f38efd5291a5660e1e2c06f6474b6073be8be13cd8689",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The Gutzwiller trace mechanism turns stationary recurrent trajectories into oscillatory spectral terms weighted by action, stability, and Maslov phase. The absorption and emission models can agree at the semiclassical counting level while differing in quantum fluctuations, where the absorption minus sign is represented by setting the Maslov phases to π; sign-sensitive phase data therefore discriminate the two proposed realizations.",
